Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/v4l2m2m: accept ENOENT from an empty event queue

The nonblocking v4l2_event_dequeue() path returns __v4l2_event_dequeue(),
which returns -ENOENT when the available-event list is empty. A real Iris
trace dequeued SOURCE_CHANGE successfully, then got errno 2 on the next
DQEVENT. Treat that result as the end of the event loop, just like EAGAIN.

Only the DQEVENT result is affected. DQBUF, poll, command and other I/O
errors remain errors; no capture ERROR or LAST flags are changed.

--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_context.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_context.c
@@ -182,8 +182,9 @@
     for (;;) {
         memset(&evt, 0, sizeof(evt));
         ret = ioctl(s->fd, VIDIOC_DQEVENT, &evt);
+        /* V4L2 core reports ENOENT for an empty nonblocking event queue. */
         if (ret < 0)
-            return errno == EAGAIN || errno == ENOTTY || errno == EINVAL ? 0 : AVERROR(errno);
+            return errno == ENOENT || errno == EAGAIN || errno == ENOTTY || errno == EINVAL ? 0 : AVERROR(errno);
 
         if (evt.type == V4L2_EVENT_EOS) {
             if (s->capture.av_codec_id != AV_CODEC_ID_RAWVIDEO)
